                    StatementSource.WithoutFormula(),
                    AssessedProvenance.FromRepo(),
                    Blocks(
                        Paragraph(Text("The preserved target quantifies over continuous even real F, arbitrary real-to-natural m with eventual m(D)>=1 and m(D)/D -> 0, and every finite complex family indexed by Fin n, with repeated nodes allowed and every moment r<m(D) annihilated. The conclusion remains: for every epsilon>0 there is C>0 such that |F(t)| <= C exp(epsilon |t|) for every real t. There is no initial exponential majorant, monotone order, fixed order, or sparse-sequence substitute.")),
                        Paragraph(Text("For integers 1<=p<=n and real r, the exact finite Newton identity is F(n+r)=sum(q<p) choose(n,q) Delta^q F(r)+sum(j=0..n-p) choose(n-1-j,p-1) Delta^p F(r+j), with unit-step forward differences. Summation by parts with weight choose(n-j,p) proves one induction step: Pascal's identity gives the remainder coefficients choose(n-1-j,p-1), and the terminal weight choose(p-1,p) is zero. The p=1 base is ordinary finite telescoping. Applying the same step to the constant sequence 1 shows that the remainder coefficients sum to choose(n,p). They are nonnegative, so termwise absolute-value bounds give the stated finite inequality, including p=n and n=p=1.")),
                        Paragraph(Text("Set w_j=(-1)^j choose(k,j), j=0..k. The k-fold finite difference kills every translated power of degree below k, so each translated stencil satisfies all required moments when k=m(D). Write G(u)=sum(i,j) w_i w_j F(u+i-j). Evenness makes G(-u)=G(u). For u>=0 and u+k<=D, apply the original complex-family positivity to the two real blocks (w_i) and (+/- w_j) at nodes i and u+j. Transporting their finite disjoint-union index to Fin(card) preserves every repeated or overlapping node. The resulting inequalities 2G(0)+/-2G(u)>=0 give |G(u)|<=G(0), including G(0)=0. The stencil l1 norm is 2^k and |i-j|<=k; continuity on [0,k] and evenness therefore give |G(0)|<=2^(2k)M(k). The exact double-stencil identity is G(u)=(-1)^k Delta^(2k)F(u-k). Thus, with u=v+k, the high-difference bound holds whenever v>=0 and v+2k<=D. No arbitrary unrelated order is admitted.")),
                        Paragraph(Text("Define M(R)=max(1,sup(x in [0,R]) |F(x)|) for nonnegative real R. Continuity makes each such compact-interval supremum finite; M is positive and monotone. In Newton's identity take p=2k, 0<=r<=1 and D=n+r with k=m(D). For q<p, the signed stencil identity bounds |Delta^q F(r)| by 2^q M(p+1). For each remainder index j<=n-p, v=r+j is nonnegative and v+p<=D, so the Gram bound gives |Delta^p F(v)|<=2^p M(k)<=2^p M(p+1). The exact nonnegative coefficient sum now yields |F(n+r)|<=M(2k+1) sum(q<=2k) 2^q choose(n,q). Eventually m(t)/t<1/8 and t>=4, so 2m(t)+1<=t/2 and 2m(t)<=floor(t). Taking n=floor(t), r=t-floor(t) and k=m(t) proves this estimate at every sufficiently large real t, without monotonicity. These are authored proof bodies; no Lean elaboration or kernel check was performed.")),
                        Paragraph(Text("The generating-function continuation uses an arbitrary auxiliary real z with 0<z<=1. Since z^p<=z^q for q<=p, multiplying the truncated positive sum by z^p bounds it by the full binomial expansion (1+2z)^n. Multiplication by z^(-p), followed by z^(-1)<=exp(z^(-1)) and 1+2z<=exp(2z), gives sum(q<=p) 2^q choose(n,q)<=exp(p/z+2nz). This deliberately nonoptimized bound has the same required o(t) consequence and uses no growth hypothesis.")),
                        Paragraph(Text("For any eta>0 choose the fixed auxiliary parameter z=min(1,eta/6). The given limit m(t)/t -> 0 makes 2m(t)<=z^2 t eventually. With p=2m(t), n=floor(t)<=t, the exponent p/z+2nz is at most 3zt<=eta t. This is uniform at every sufficiently large real t. The auxiliary z is fixed only after eta is chosen; the moment order remains the original arbitrary m(t). Together with 2m(t)+1<=t/2 and compact-envelope monotonicity, the finite Newton estimate yields |F(t)|<=M(t/2)exp(eta t).")),
                        Paragraph(Text("Choose T>0 beyond that uniform threshold. For R>=2T, each t in [0,R] with t<=T is bounded by M(R/2), while t>T is bounded by M(t/2)exp(eta t)<=M(R/2)exp(eta R). Since M(R/2)>=1 and exp(eta R)>=1, taking the finite compact-interval supremum gives M(R)<=M(R/2)exp(eta R), including the max with 1. Induction on finite depth N for 0<=R<=2T*2^N gives M(R)<=M(2T)exp(2eta R); the base uses monotonicity and the induction step combines the half-radius exponent eta R with eta R. Powers of 2 are unbounded, so every finite nonnegative R is covered. This is the finite geometric-sum bound, without any infinite supremum or initial exponential majorant.")),
                        Paragraph(Text("Set eta=epsilon/2 and C=M(2T)>0. Apply the real-radius bound at R=|t| and use evenness to obtain the original conclusion for every real t. The sole public theorem is sublinear_moment_growth; its complete F,m,continuity,evenness,eventual-positive-order,sublinear-limit,and finite-complex-family telescope and proof body are unchanged. The unused originalTheorem proposition packaging and the unconsumed duplicate alias original_theorem are removed from the replayed candidate. This changes only the target representation, not any mathematical clause. The consumed momentPositive definition retains the exact original finite-family premise; all proof helpers remain private. Every proof body is an unelaborated source candidate.")),
                        Paragraph(Text("The separate owner Reg/D5/S3/Analytic/Interpolation/SublinearMomentGrowth.lean imports the analytic source, Contract.Registration and Reg.Support.SingleDependentReadout under the existing Reg package graph, with explicit noncomputable, Filter, Real, finite-sum, conjugation and topology context. D5 imports no audit package, and no package, tool or judge is changed. The old optional same-unit registration-attempt patch is retained as an immutable predecessor but is excluded from replay; its Reg mathematical bodies are reused in the new owner. The four-slot Contract.Registration targets the unapplied full sublinear_moment_growth term with Realization signature, Unit and Unit carriers. Its arena observes the whole real function through the existing enrolled DependentFamily.realize template and retains every original binder and premise. The actual readout is identity. The rejected readout is exp(2|t|); the original hypotheses are satisfied by F=0,m=1, but its epsilon=1 conclusion would force exp(C+1)<=C, contradicting C+2<=exp(C+1). Authored rejected-law, whole-family sensitivity and observational-dependence terms and the Iff.rfl bridge are preserved. An explicit sourceSelection selects the literal F operand within the concluded |F t|: it crosses all nine outer binders, Exists C, its right conjunct and forall t; lexical state binder 0 is the entire original F, with no parameter coordinates, function-operand mode or replacement state operand. This authors the identity observation rather than assuming automatic reconstruction; its raw path, exact whole-telescope reconstruction, enrollment recognition, typed fields and all proof terms remain unassessed until canonical compilation and faithful compiled audit. familyRecord is none for direct.source and continuation remains unknown. The arithmetic supplier of m(D)=o(D) remains unproved. No RH, Reg validation, kernel, freeze, CI or official acceptance is claimed."))),
